    "## Ethics \n",
    "\n",
    "Instructions: Keep the contents of this cell. For each item on the checklist\n",
    "-  put an X there if you've considered the item\n",
    "-  IF THE ITEM IS RELEVANT place a short paragraph after the checklist item discussing the issue.\n",
    "  \n",
    "Items on this checklist are meant to provoke discussion among good-faith actors who take their ethical responsibilities seriously. Your teams will document these discussions and decisions for posterity using this section.  You don't have to solve these problems, you just have to acknowledge any potential harm no matter how unlikely.\n",
    "\n",
    "Here is a [list of real world examples](https://deon.drivendata.org/examples/) for each item in the checklist that can refer to.\n",
    "\n",
    "[![Deon badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/ethics%20checklist-deon-brightgreen.svg?style=popout-square)](http://deon.drivendata.org/)\n",
    "\n",
    "### A. Data Collection\n",
" - [ ] **A.1 Informed consent**: If there are human subjects, have they given informed consent, where subjects affirmatively opt-in and have a clear understanding of the data uses to which they consent?\n",
"   This project does not involve direct human subjects. We use publicly available aggregated datasets, so informed consent is not applicable.\n",
"\n",
" - [X] **A.2 Collection bias**: Have we considered sources of bias that could be introduced during data collection and survey design and taken steps to mitigate those?\n",
"   The datasets may include bias due to self-reported health data and limitations in food access measurement. We acknowledge these biases in our analysis.\n",
"\n",
" - [X] **A.3 Limit PII exposure**: Have we considered ways to minimize exposure of personally identifiable information (PII)?\n",
"   The data is aggregated and contains no personally identifiable information, so PII exposure is minimal.\n",
"\n",
" - [X] **A.4 Downstream bias mitigation**: Have we considered ways to enable testing downstream results for biased outcomes?\n",
"   We consider how our results may reflect systemic inequalities and interpret findings carefully to avoid reinforcing harmful stereotypes.\n",
"\n",

"### B. Data Storage\n",
" - [X] **B.1 Data security**: Do we have a plan to protect and secure data?\n",
"   We store publicly available data in secure environments and avoid modifying raw data in ways that could introduce errors.\n",
"\n",
" - [ ] **B.2 Right to be forgotten**: Do we have a mechanism through which an individual can request their personal information be removed?\n",
"   This does not apply because the data contains no personal identifiers.\n",
"\n",
" - [X] **B.3 Data retention plan**: Is there a schedule or plan to delete the data after it is no longer needed?\n",
"   The data will be kept only for the duration of the project and can be re-downloaded from original sources if needed.\n",
"\n",

"### C. Analysis\n",
" - [X] **C.1 Missing perspectives**: Have we sought to address blindspots in the analysis?\n",
"   Our analysis may not capture all social or cultural factors, so we interpret results cautiously.\n",
"\n",
" - [X] **C.2 Dataset bias**: Have we examined the data for possible sources of bias?\n",
"   We recognize possible biases such as self-reporting errors and missing variables and avoid overgeneralizing.\n",
"\n",
" - [X] **C.3 Honest representation**: Are our visualizations designed to honestly represent the data?\n",
"   We ensure visualizations accurately reflect the data without distortion or misleading scaling.\n",
"\n",
" - [X] **C.4 Privacy in analysis**: Have we ensured that data with PII are not used?\n",
"   No personally identifiable information is used in our analysis.\n",
"\n",
" - [X] **C.5 Auditability**: Is the process well documented and reproducible?\n",
"   Our analysis steps are documented in the notebook so the work can be reproduced.\n",
"\n",

"### D. Modeling\n",
" - [X] **D.1 Proxy discrimination**: Have we ensured that the model does not rely on discriminatory proxies?\n",
"   We acknowledge that variables like income may act as proxies and interpret results carefully.\n",
"\n",
" - [ ] **D.2 Fairness across groups**: Have we tested model results for fairness?\n",
"   We are not building a predictive model, so formal fairness testing does not apply.\n",
"\n",
" - [ ] **D.3 Metric selection**: Have we considered the effects of optimizing for metrics?\n",
"   We are not optimizing a predictive model, so this is not applicable.\n",
"\n",
" - [X] **D.4 Explainability**: Can we explain model decisions in understandable terms?\n",
"   Our analysis is based on simple statistical relationships that are easy to interpret.\n",
"\n",
" - [X] **D.5 Communicate limitations**: Have we communicated shortcomings and biases?\n",
"   We clearly state that our findings show correlation, not causation, and discuss dataset limitations.\n",
"\n",

"### E. Deployment\n",
" - [ ] **E.1 Monitoring and evaluation**: Do we have a plan to monitor the model after deployment?\n",
"   This project is not deployed as a system, so monitoring is not applicable.\n",
"\n",
" - [ ] **E.2 Redress**: Do we have a plan for response if users are harmed?\n",
"   There is no deployment, so harm response mechanisms are not needed.\n",
"\n",
" - [ ] **E.3 Roll back**: Is there a way to turn off or roll back the model?\n",
"   No deployed model exists, so rollback is not applicable.\n",
"\n",
" - [ ] **E.4 Unintended use**: Have we taken steps to prevent unintended uses?\n",
"   While not deployed, we present results carefully to reduce risk of misinterpretation.\n",
